## Summary

- assign the canonical tax owner operation before read-policy admission;
- route `TaxCalculationPort::calculate_tax` admission through one tax-owned helper using the unchanged `PortCallPolicy::read()` contract;
- retain truthful `rustok_tax` owner context for deadline and policy rejection, including correlation id, tenant, actor, channel, locale, causation id, traceparent, idempotency key, deadline, exact operation, original code/kind/retryability, and the stable `tax_calculation_port` boundary;
- use error severity for unavailable, timeout, and invariant failures and warning severity for ordinary rejection;
- rethrow the original `PortError` unchanged after diagnostics;
- preserve tax request/result validation, service delegation, DTOs, stable public validation/invariant messages, and existing test source;
- add a focused policy-context guard, align the existing tax error-context verifier with the shared helper, and add a source-ready/unvalidated evidence note.

## Scope

Four files only:

- `crates/rustok-tax/src/ports.rs`
- `scripts/verify/verify-tax-calculation-policy-context.mjs`
- `scripts/verify/verify-tax-calculation-error-context.mjs`
- `crates/rustok-tax/docs/calculation-port-policy-context.md`

## Plan alignment

This advances the still-open ecommerce P0 correlation-safe tax mapper cleanup. It closes the owner-side gap where tax read-policy/deadline rejection occurred before the owner operation was assigned or a tax-specific structured event was emitted. Consumer-side tax transport context and remaining promotion, compensation, order, payment, fulfillment, inventory, customer, and ecommerce adapters remain open. No FBA/FFA status is promoted.

## Validation

- branch is one clean commit ahead of current `main` and zero commits behind;
- diff contains exactly the four scoped files;
- owner operation assignment precedes policy admission and request validation;
- the helper performs the unchanged read-policy check, logs the full available context, and rethrows the original error;
- stable tax request, provider-result, and service validation envelopes remain unchanged;
- the existing tax error-context verifier is synchronized with the new helper rather than retaining a stale inline-admission expectation;
- concurrent `main` changes touched only Index and Notifications/Forum files and did not overlap this slice;
- tests, Cargo commands, formatting commands, verifier execution, workflow checks, and CI were not run, per maintainer instruction.

Suggested focused checks:

```bash
node scripts/verify/verify-tax-calculation-policy-context.mjs
node scripts/verify/verify-tax-calculation-error-context.mjs
node scripts/verify/verify-ecommerce-public-port-error-safety-v2.mjs
cargo check -p rustok-tax --lib
```

Internal PR #2256 was used only to delete a superseded technical branch. The final branch was rebuilt directly from current `main`; its temporary handoff file and staging history are absent from this PR.

## Objet

En cas d’échec du finaliseur temporaire, enregistrer uniquement les 120 dernières lignes utiles dans `.tmp/ch14/last-error.txt` sur la branche documentaire.

## Garanties

- les modifications documentaires partielles sont désindexées avant le commit de diagnostic ;
- seul le fichier de diagnostic temporaire est poussé ;
- sa suppression est ajoutée à la liste fermée du lot final ;
- aucune donnée sensible ni secret n’est attendu dans ce journal de validation documentaire ;
- le mécanisme reste temporaire et sera supprimé par la PR #301.

## Scope

Implements `ASSET-BUILDINGS` from accepted Audit PR #101.

- processed and registered 72 approved building images;
- added deterministic mechanical/runtime bindings and generated browser lookup;
- routed planet building cards and facility backgrounds through the complete resolver;
- removed migrated building-card atlas and post-render replacement assumptions;
- added six dark/light QA contact sheets and complete 72-ID coverage;
- preserved gameplay, balance, bots and save schema.

## Validation

- asset freshness and budget checks passed;
- lint and strict TypeScript passed;
- 307 tests passed;
- production build passed;
- Graphify audit passed.

## Étage 9B

- contexte limité à l’organisation et à l’utilisateur autorisés;
- minimisation explicite des champs;
- provenance et période de validité conservées;
- refus des références interorganisation;
- tests contractuels.

Dépend de #245.
Closes part of #195.

## Scope

Implement bounded PRS-002B tracked by #148.

Included:
- internally synchronized `PlayerPersistenceState`;
- SaveManager-owned state keyed by exact `weak_ptr` ownership identity rather than GUID;
- one in-flight asynchronous save generation per exact Player object;
- coalescing of newer explicit online save requests;
- exact success/failure acknowledgement after persistence result;
- one follow-up save after success when a newer requested generation remains dirty;
- failure remains dirty without automatic retry;
- removal of GUID/timestamp coalescing from per-player async scheduling;
- deterministic concurrency and source-contract tests.

## Safety boundaries

- dirty generation represents accepted explicit `savePlayer` requests only in this slice;
- no broad gameplay mutation instrumentation;
- no change to saveAll, offline/shutdown synchronous saves or server-wide timestamp scheduling;
- no automatic retry, backoff, metrics backend, database/schema/deployment change, PRS-003 outage state or PRS-004 fencing;
- no RPO claim.

## Validation

- compact checkpoint validator;
- state concurrency tests and SaveManager source-contract tests;
- exact-head full repository CI and `Required`;
- final six-path discussion and main-drift audit.

## Problème
Les correctifs successifs avaient rendu le dialogue vocal trop complexe : détection de volume, création WAV, transcription Gemini, réponse puis TTS. Cela ajoutait plusieurs points de panne et la voix pouvait basculer silencieusement vers Windows ou le navigateur.

## Nouvelle architecture
- reconnaissance vocale continue native Edge/Chrome en français ;
- aucun push-to-talk et aucune calibration WAV ;
- mot d’appel « Mairaiy » détecté directement dans la transcription ;
- envoi immédiat du texte à Aura Live via `/api/voice/text` ;
- réponse textuelle retournée avant la fin du TTS ;
- génération vocale suivie séparément dans `/api/voice/status` ;
- reprise automatique de l’écoute après la fin réelle de sa voix.

## Identité vocale
- voix publique verrouillée sur `Leda` via `MAIRAIY_LOCKED_VOICE` ;
- aucun repli automatique Windows ou navigateur ;
- en cas d’échec Gemini ou de plafond TTS, Mairaiy reste silencieuse au lieu de changer de timbre ;
- l’overlay refuse aussi le fallback navigateur si un fichier Gemini ne peut pas être lu.

## Runtime
- nouveau point d’entrée `app.main_v3` ;
- démarrage direct par Uvicorn pour éviter une double importation ;
- diagnostics enrichis avec état temps réel, tâche vocale, durée et erreur de voix.

## Tests
- dialogue texte → réponse → voix ;
- phrase sans mot d’appel ignorée ;
- impossibilité de basculer automatiquement sur Windows ;
- validation Python, tests et syntaxe JavaScript via CI.

Closes #29.

## What changed
- rebuilds all 25 encrypted calendar-linked pages with three concrete place blocks and three local image assets per page;
- removes arithmetic/fake map coordinates and generic “Головні райони / Локальні враження” labels;
- shows a place-specific image beside every concrete place block;
- uses exact named Google Maps destinations and hides the fake embedded map;
- keeps five broad research comparisons route-less until an itinerary is selected;
- fixes GitHub Pages publication so `calendar-trips-2026/**` is synchronized from `main` to `gh-pages`;
- preserves the existing fragment key, trip IDs, and Calendar deep-links.

## Validation
- decrypted payload contains exactly 25 trips;
- 75 image references resolve to 75 repository assets;
- each trip has three distinct asset paths;
- 69 unique image files overall; the six intentional repeats are the shared Milan place set across three Milan date variants;
- no arithmetic points, old Unsplash set, generic placeholder labels, or truncated-output corruption;
- loader JavaScript passes `node --check` and repository diff passes `git diff --check`.

`pytest` is unavailable in the execution image; targeted structural/decryption validation passed.
